{"authority_class":"PLATFORM","conditions":[],"extraction":{"method":"authored-span-annotations","version":"concurrency-semantics.v1"},"formalization":"DESCRIPTIVE: github.head_ref is defined only for event = pull_request; elsewhere a group using it without a fallback is a syntax error; the fallback ${{ github.head_ref || github.run_id }} yields the run id.","heading_ancestry":["Example: Using a fallback value"],"id":"semantic-occurrence:532d566b178213f7dde32d807bc36d2a5a0d033f22cdd8f70c949cdeb2cc9e88","include_chain":["data/reusables/actions/jobs/section-using-concurrency.md","data/reusables/actions/jobs/section-using-concurrency-jobs.md"],"page_applications":[],"products":["GitHub Actions"],"review":{"evidence_reference":null,"reviewer":null,"status":"PROPOSED"},"schema":"ges.semantic-occurrence.v1","semantic_ast":{"action":"be","consequences":[],"exceptions":["the run ID is unique and defined for every run"],"modality":"DESCRIPTIVE","object":"defined only on pull_request events, so other events need a fallback such as the run ID to avoid a syntax error","parameters":[],"polarity":"POSITIVE","preconditions":[],"qualifiers":[],"scope":["github/docs","data/reusables/actions/actions-group-concurrency.md"],"subject":"github.head_ref"},"semantic_kind":"FACT","source":{"commit":"56fcfa816f27bca239e5d39fff0d4f74f77ec995","content_sha256":"3b099dc5cc26dfc0fe2dcf88afd9ad70f10957911bd2fbc6ba2815e8417642e9","end_line":148,"path":"data/reusables/actions/actions-group-concurrency.md","repository":"github/docs","span_sha256":"99011d4fa56cd6c6508eb054212ad06f181dd77f1554919612dc4acc662de408","start_line":148},"versions":[]}
{"authority_class":"PLATFORM","conditions":[],"extraction":{"method":"authored-span-annotations","version":"concurrency-semantics.v1"},"formalization":"CONSTRAINT: a group is keyed by repository and name, not by workflow; two workflows with one group name share it. A newer run replaces an older pending run in that group; an in-progress run is canceled only when its workflow sets cancel-in-progress: true. Including github.workflow in the group name keeps workflows apart.","heading_ancestry":["Example: Only cancel in-progress jobs or runs for the current workflow"],"id":"semantic-occurrence:b1b3c7660476c17ffbb7635f20095aa4e3d51b42ff1f2856a9dbc012ac9eab0a","include_chain":["data/reusables/actions/jobs/section-using-concurrency.md","data/reusables/actions/jobs/section-using-concurrency-jobs.md"],"page_applications":[],"products":["GitHub Actions"],"review":{"evidence_reference":null,"reviewer":null,"status":"PROPOSED"},"schema":"ges.semantic-occurrence.v1","semantic_ast":{"action":"be","consequences":[],"exceptions":[],"modality":"DESCRIPTIVE","object":"unique across workflows in a repository, otherwise any previous in-progress or pending job is canceled regardless of the workflow","parameters":[],"polarity":"POSITIVE","preconditions":[],"qualifiers":[],"scope":["github/docs","data/reusables/actions/actions-group-concurrency.md"],"subject":"concurrency group names"},"semantic_kind":"CONSTRAINT","source":{"commit":"56fcfa816f27bca239e5d39fff0d4f74f77ec995","content_sha256":"3b099dc5cc26dfc0fe2dcf88afd9ad70f10957911bd2fbc6ba2815e8417642e9","end_line":162,"path":"data/reusables/actions/actions-group-concurrency.md","repository":"github/docs","span_sha256":"75f72393dd4a067d5f686577bf08190e02a09f50eedf8f045c22962455f9bc70","start_line":162},"versions":[]}
{"authority_class":"PLATFORM","conditions":[],"extraction":{"method":"authored-span-annotations","version":"concurrency-semantics.v1"},"formalization":"DESCRIPTIVE: with cancel-in-progress = !contains(github.ref, 'release/'), pushes to a release branch do not cancel in-progress runs; pushes to other branches do.","heading_ancestry":["Example: Only cancel in-progress jobs on specific branches"],"id":"semantic-occurrence:172d8f8f49b1ac6e228d2dc7c27d8098bee5c1b30181cd035f2c0d9a849db53b","include_chain":["data/reusables/actions/jobs/section-using-concurrency.md","data/reusables/actions/jobs/section-using-concurrency-jobs.md"],"page_applications":[],"products":["GitHub Actions"],"review":{"evidence_reference":null,"reviewer":null,"status":"PROPOSED"},"schema":"ges.semantic-occurrence.v1","semantic_ast":{"action":"cancel","consequences":[],"exceptions":["pushes to a release/ branch do not cancel in-progress runs"],"modality":"DESCRIPTIVE","object":"in-progress runs on non-release branches only","parameters":[],"polarity":"POSITIVE","preconditions":[],"qualifiers":[],"scope":["github/docs","data/reusables/actions/actions-group-concurrency.md"],"subject":"cancel-in-progress as an expression"},"semantic_kind":"FACT","source":{"commit":"56fcfa816f27bca239e5d39fff0d4f74f77ec995","content_sha256":"3b099dc5cc26dfc0fe2dcf88afd9ad70f10957911bd2fbc6ba2815e8417642e9","end_line":192,"path":"data/reusables/actions/actions-group-concurrency.md","repository":"github/docs","span_sha256":"b7cf953ec7a3547dd9be6ee1608f08f3e19fc8c65707be8af41d4ccdc4ae4840","start_line":192},"versions":[]}
